# RU(a - b) for the public building block kairn::sub_up (milestone2.md, "Values that enter from
# the program"): both operands pass through guard, then sub_up_1. The statement is sub_up_1's, in
# both models; not claimed: the sign of a zero result, which the guard can change.
kernel:        sub_up_entry
input:         a
input:         b
output:        r
value:         a-b
ensures:       rounded r up
min_precision: 2
source:        sub_up_1 on its guarded operands (Milestone 2 listing)
license:       algorithm and proof: MIT
theorem:       proofs/theories/DirectedSum.v sub_up_entry_correct
status:        proved
domain:        extended
ieee_status:   proved
ieee_theorem:  proofs/theories/IeeeEntry.v sub_up_entry_ieee_correct
entry:         yes
cone_exempt:   through sub_up_1, whose result is selected; the rounded claim states the output for infinite and NaN operands

ga = guard(a)
gb = guard(b)
r  = sub_up_1(ga, gb)
